          "System age changes the talk track. A five-year system is a repair until proven otherwise. A twenty-year R-22 leftover is a replacement conversation even if they called for a 'quick fix.' Don't force the CSR to upsell on a cost-per-call that's priced like a capacitor. If you want replacement-intent only, say so and accept lower volume. If you want all service, accept mixed tickets.",
          "Access and safety: attic units in August, crawlspaces, dogs, locked gates, HOA rules about parking the truck. You won't get all of that on a 90-second transfer. Get the landmines. 'Is the unit in the attic?' saves a tech who showed up in jeans. 'Is anyone home between 1 and 5?' saves a wasted roll.",
